Title: rtk hook fails to run pytest (spawn error)
Created: 2026-06-17
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-06-17T11:14Z Minh Ha-Duong created

--- body ---
## Context
With the `rtk hook claude` Bash PreToolUse hook active, `pytest` and
`python3 -m pytest` are rewritten by rtk and fail:

    rtk: Failed to run pytest: Failed to spawn process: No such file or directory (os error 2)

The pytest binary exists (`~/.local/bin/pytest`; `python3 -c "import pytest"`
works), so the rtk-spawned child cannot resolve it on its PATH. Working
workaround: `rtk proxy python3 -m pytest …` bypasses the rewrite and runs the
suite normally (verified 2026-06-17 on the `~/CNRS/html` test suite — 65 passed).

`rtk config.toml` (default, at `~/.config/rtk/config.toml`, uncreated) has **no
command-passthrough / allowlist knob** — its sections are tracking, display,
filters (output ignore globs), and tee. So the root fix is in the **rtk binary**
(an external tool), not this repo. This ticket is the harness-side record +
decision on where to land the fix.

## Relevant files
- `settings.json` — the `rtk hook claude` Bash matcher (~line 168). **Do not
  edit blindly**: another session held `settings.json` and `scripts/shell-init.sh`
  dirty on 2026-06-17 (unrelated changes); coordinate before touching.
- `~/.config/rtk/config.toml` — default, no relevant knob.
- rtk binary (external repo) — actual rewrite logic.
- `rules/coding-python.md` — candidate home for a documented workaround.

## Actions
1. Decide the fix locus:
   a. Patch/report rtk so its pytest rewrite resolves the binary via
      `python -m pytest` or honours the caller's PATH; or
   b. add a pytest passthrough/allowlist if rtk gains one; or
   c. if neither is available, document `rtk proxy python3 -m pytest` as the
      standing workaround.
2. If (c): add a one-line note to the Testing section of `rules/coding-python.md`.

## Test
- Reproduce: run `python3 -m pytest` under the hook → observe the spawn failure.
- Confirm `rtk proxy python3 -m pytest` succeeds on the same suite.

## Verification
- [ ] pytest runs cleanly under the hook (rtk fixed) OR the `rtk proxy`
      workaround is documented where a Python test-writer will see it.

## Invariants
- Do not break other rtk command rewrites.
- Do not edit `settings.json` / `scripts/shell-init.sh` while another session
  holds them dirty.

## Exit criteria
- Either pytest runs under the hook, or the workaround is documented and
  discoverable; the ticket records the rtk-side root cause.
